{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md && git show --stat --oneline 18a7731 5e201e0 858a190 81dd75e 1221d86 && git show --format=fuller --no-ext-diff 81dd75e && git diff --stat 18a7731\"'^..HEAD && git diff --no-ext-diff 18a7731''^..HEAD'","aggregated_output":"# T-102 — /health reports approvals summary\n\nState: In progress\nBranch: ticket/T-102-health-approvals-summary\nRisk class: low (read-only endpoint, no external actions)\n\n## Description\n\nT-101 gave operators queue counts on `GET /health`. The other thing an operator checks at a glance is the approvals pipeline: how many proposed actions are waiting for a human, and how the closed ones ended. Extend `GET /health` to also report approvals counts by status.\n\nThe approval statuses in `conformance/app/server.js` are: `pending`, `sent`, `rejected`, `blocked_recipient`. The existing `ok` and `queue` fields must not change (T-101's tests stay green).\n\n## Acceptance criteria (planner freezes the exact contract)\n\n1. On a fresh server, `/health` reports zero approvals in every status. → satisfied when the response body matches Frozen contract §\"Fresh server\" exactly.\n2. After a job completes and proposes an action, `/health` shows one pending approval. → satisfied when the response body matches Frozen contract §\"One pending approval\" exactly.\n3. After that approval is approved, `/health` shows it under sent, and pending returns to zero. → satisfied when the response body matches Frozen contract §\"Approved\" exactly.\n\n## Frozen contract\n\n`GET /health` gains an `approvals` field alongside the existing `ok` and `queue` fields (unchanged, per T-101). Response is `200 OK`, `Content-Type: application/json`.\n\nShape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"queue\": { \"pending\": 0, \"done\": 0, \"dead\": 0 },\n  \"approvals\": { \"pending\": 0, \"sent\": 0, \"rejected\": 0, \"blocked_recipient\": 0 }\n}\n```\n\n- `approvals` has exactly these four keys, always present, in this order, values are non-negative integers counting `state.approvals` entries by `.status` (statuses defined in `conformance/app/server.js`: `pending`, `sent`, `rejected`, `blocked_recipient`).\n- No other keys are added to `approvals`. No existing key of the top-level response (`ok`, `queue`) changes shape or meaning.\n\nAcceptance criterion → exact expected body:\n\n1. **Fresh server** (AC1) — no events posted yet:\n   ```json\n   { \"ok\": true, \"queue\": { \"pending\": 0, \"done\": 0, \"dead\": 0 }, \"approvals\": { \"pending\": 0, \"sent\": 0, \"rejected\": 0, \"blocked_recipient\": 0 } }\n   ```\n\n2. **One pending approval** (AC2) — after posting an event and waiting for its job to reach `done` (which produces one approval in `pending`):\n   ```json\n   { \"ok\": true, \"queue\": { \"pending\": 0, \"done\": 1, \"dead\": 0 }, \"approvals\": { \"pending\": 1, \"sent\": 0, \"rejected\": 0, \"blocked_recipient\": 0 } }\n   ```\n\n3. **Approved** (AC3) — after `POST /api/approvals/:id/approve` on that approval (recipient on allowlist, so it succeeds):\n   ```json\n   { \"ok\": true, \"queue\": { \"pending\": 0, \"done\": 1, \"dead\": 0 }, \"approvals\": { \"pending\": 0, \"sent\": 1, \"rejected\": 0, \"blocked_recipient\": 0 } }\n   ```\n\nIf this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- App lives in `conformance/app/` (zero-dependency Node 18+; see `conformance/SPEC.md`).\n- Tests go in `conformance/app/tests/` — new file `tests/health-approvals.test.js`, same style as the existing suites (node:test, spawn the real server on its own port with a temp DATA_DIR).\n- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/health-approvals.test.js`.\n\n## Log\n\n- 2026-07-12: ticket created by the operator; State → Ready. First ticket to be dispatched by Hermes (dispatcher trial).\n- 2026-07-12: planner froze `GET /health` `approvals` contract and mapped acceptance criteria to exact response bodies.\n- 2026-07-12 21:01:57: planner run completed through the wrapper; contract frozen in commit `8f0bc25`; State → In progress; cost $0.3306252.\n- 2026-07-12 21:06:49: test-author run completed through the wrapper; 3 contract tests committed in `18a7731`, all failing for the expected missing `approvals` field (0 passed, 3 failed); cost $0.2296.\n- 2026-07-12: builder implemented the frozen contract exactly (added `approvals` counts to the `/health` handler in `conformance/app/server.js`). `tests/health-approvals.test.js` (3/3) passes with exact `JSON.stringify` matches, confirming the implementation matches the frozen contract. **Blocked before commit:** this breaks all 4 pre-existing T-101 tests in `tests/health.test.js` (tests 1, 1b, 2, 3), which assert the `/health` body with `assert.deepStrictEqual(...)` against object literals that have no `approvals` key — `deepStrictEqual` rejects any extra key, so adding `approvals` anywhere in the response necessarily fails them. This is not an implementation bug: no server-side change can satisfy both \"exact frozen `approvals` shape per AC1–3\" and \"T-101's `health.test.js` stays green,\" because the latter was written before this contract existed and asserts an exact object with no extra keys. Per the builder's no-test-editing rule, I have not touched `tests/health.test.js` or any other test file, and have not committed the (correct, but suite-red) implementation change. Flagging for re-planning/reviewer adjudication: either (a) the contract stands and `health.test.js`'s 4 assertions need updating by the test-author/reviewer to tolerate/expect the new `approvals` key, or (b) the contract needs to change. Full suite as of this run: 11 passed, 4 failed (all 4 failures are the `health.test.js` ones described above; `health-approvals.test.js` and `conformance.test.js` are fully green).\n- 2026-07-12 21:10:01: builder run completed through the wrapper and committed implementation plus its ticket note in `5e201e0`; new contract tests pass 3/3 but the full suite is red (11 passed, 4 pre-existing T-101 health tests failed); State → Blocked-Escalated; cost $0.6861495. Javier must decide whether the frozen additive contract stands and authorize test-author updates to `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js`, or send T-102 back to planner for a revised contract.\n- 2026-07-12: operator decision — the frozen additive T-102 contract stands; test-author is authorized to update only the exact-match `/health` expectations in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js` to include the frozen `approvals` object; State → In progress.\n- 2026-07-12: dispatch stopped because mandatory `next-stage.sh --ticket T-102` returned `RUN reviewer`, not `RUN test-author`; State → Blocked-Escalated. Javier must reconcile the sequencer/bookkeeping so it names the authorized test-author correction; no role run was launched.\n- 2026-07-12: operator resolution — no state surgery is needed; the frozen additive contract stands, the stale pre-T-102 exact-match assertions in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js` are the fault, and `RUN reviewer` is the legal adjudication step; State → In progress.\n- 2026-07-12 21:14:32: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — update only the four stale exact-match `/health` expected bodies in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js` to include the frozen `approvals` object with scenario-appropriate counts; implementation and new tests conform; cost $0.1776.\n- 2026-07-12: dispatch refused before the authorized test-author fix because the mandatory sequencer reported `REFUSE reviewer ran 1 time(s) but only 0 verdict(s) are logged on /Users/sofiagonzalez/Projects/software-factory/conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md`; the verdict exists on the ticket branch in `a2aba87`, but the dispatcher cannot write it to main; State → Blocked-Escalated. Javier must reconcile the main ticket bookkeeping or sequencer source; no role run was launched.\n- 2026-07-12: operator resolution — during T-102 runs, ticket bookkeeping is read from the ticket worktree while the ledger remains in the factory repo; use `FACTORY_ROOT=~/Projects/sf-worktrees/T-102/conformance` with `FACTORY_LEDGER=~/Projects/software-factory/conformance/factory/ledger.csv` for the rest of T-102; State → In progress.\n- 2026-07-12 21:17:55: test-author fix run completed through the wrapper; commit `81dd75e` changed only the four stale exact-match expectations in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js`; full suite green (15 passed, 0 failed); cost $0.1672.\n18a7731 test: pin health approvals summary contract\n conformance/app/tests/health-approvals.test.js | 106 +++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 106 insertions(+)\n5e201e0 T-102: implement approvals summary on GET /health; flag T-101 test conflict\n conformance/app/server.js            | 4 +++-\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md | 1 +\n 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n858a190 Record T-102 operator contract decision\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md | 3 ++-\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n81dd75e T-102: update health expectations for approvals summary\n conformance/app/tests/health.test.js | 4 ++++\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)\n1221d86 Log T-102 test-author fix completion\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md | 1 +\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\ncommit 81dd75e4bad4211e78995fea64b9a3693f485f21\nAuthor:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nAuthorDate: Sun Jul 12 21:17:52 2026 -0600\nCommit:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nCommitDate: Sun Jul 12 21:17:52 2026 -0600\n\n    T-102: update health expectations for approvals summary\n\ndiff --git a/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js b/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js\nindex cc106e5..9cd4e0e 100644\n--- a/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js\n+++ b/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js\n@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ test(\"1. on a fresh server, /health reports an empty queue\", async () => {\n   assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n     ok: true,\n     queue: { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 },\n+    approvals: { pending: 0, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n   });\n });\n \n@@ -83,6 +84,7 @@ test(\"1b. after an event is accepted, /health reports queue.pending incremented\n     assert.deepStrictEqual(await (await fetch(`${pendingBase}/health`)).json(), {\n       ok: true,\n       queue: { pending: 1, done: 0, dead: 0 },\n+      approvals: { pending: 0, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n     });\n   } finally {\n     pendingProc.kill(\"SIGKILL\");\n@@ -97,6 +99,7 @@ test(\"2. after a job completes, /health reports queue.done incremented by 1\", as\n   assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\n     ok: true,\n     queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 0 },\n+    approvals: { pending: 1, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n   });\n });\n \n@@ -107,5 +110,6 @@ test(\"3. after a job exhausts retries, /health reports queue.dead incremented by\n   assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\n     ok: true,\n     queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 1 },\n+    approvals: { pending: 1, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n   });\n });\n conformance/app/server.js                      |   4 +-\n conformance/app/tests/health-approvals.test.js | 106 +++++++++++++++++++++++++\n conformance/app/tests/health.test.js           |   4 +\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md           |  10 +++\n 4 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\ndiff --git a/conformance/app/server.js b/conformance/app/server.js\nindex daa8dc1..6749358 100644\n--- a/conformance/app/server.js\n+++ b/conformance/app/server.js\n@@ -144,7 +144,9 @@ const server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\n     if (req.method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/health\") {\n       const queue = { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 };\n       for (const j of state.jobs) if (j.status in queue) queue[j.status] += 1;\n-      return json(res, 200, { ok: true, queue });\n+      const approvals = { pending: 0, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 };\n+      for (const a of state.approvals) if (a.status in approvals) approvals[a.status] += 1;\n+      return json(res, 200, { ok: true, queue, approvals });\n     }\n     if (req.method === \"POST\" && url.pathname === \"/webhook/event\") {\n       const body = await readBody(req);\ndiff --git a/conformance/app/tests/health-approvals.test.js b/conformance/app/tests/health-approvals.test.js\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..6ae7ce5\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/conformance/app/tests/health-approvals.test.js\n@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@\n+const { test } = require(\"node:test\");\n+const assert = require(\"node:assert\");\n+const { spawn } = require(\"node:child_process\");\n+const fs = require(\"node:fs\");\n+const path = require(\"node:path\");\n+const os = require(\"node:os\");\n+\n+const SERVER = path.join(__dirname, \"..\", \"server.js\");\n+\n+async function withServer(port, run) {\n+  const base = `http://localhost:${port}`;\n+  const dataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"relay-health-approvals-test-\"));\n+  const proc = spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\n+    env: {\n+      ...process.env,\n+      PORT: String(port),\n+      DATA_DIR: dataDir,\n+      WORKER_MS: \"50\",\n+      ALLOWLIST: \"test@example.com\",\n+    },\n+    stdio: \"ignore\",\n+  });\n+\n+  try {\n+    for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n+      try {\n+        if ((await fetch(`${base}/health`)).ok) break;\n+      } catch { /* not up yet */ }\n+      if (i === 49) throw new Error(\"server did not come up\");\n+      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n+    }\n+    await run(base);\n+  } finally {\n+    proc.kill(\"SIGKILL\");\n+    fs.rmSync(dataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+async function post(base, pathname, body = {}) {\n+  return fetch(base + pathname, {\n+    method: \"POST\",\n+    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n+    body: JSON.stringify(body),\n+  });\n+}\n+\n+async function waitForApproval(base, id, tries = 60) {\n+  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\n+    const state = await (await fetch(`${base}/api/state`)).json();\n+    if (state.approvals.some(approval => approval.id === id)) return;\n+    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n+  }\n+  throw new Error(`approval ${id} was not proposed`);\n+}\n+\n+async function assertHealth(base, expected) {\n+  const response = await fetch(`${base}/health`);\n+  assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n+  assert.strictEqual(response.headers.get(\"content-type\"), \"application/json\");\n+  assert.strictEqual(await response.text(), JSON.stringify(expected));\n+}\n+\n+test(\"1. Fresh server\", async () => {\n+  await withServer(4731, async base => {\n+    await assertHealth(base, {\n+      ok: true,\n+      queue: { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 },\n+      approvals: { pending: 0, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n+    });\n+  });\n+});\n+\n+test(\"2. One pending approval\", async () => {\n+  await withServer(4732, async base => {\n+    await post(base, \"/webhook/event\", {\n+      id: \"health-one-pending\",\n+      payload: { to: \"test@example.com\" },\n+    });\n+    await waitForApproval(base, \"appr-health-one-pending\");\n+\n+    await assertHealth(base, {\n+      ok: true,\n+      queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 0 },\n+      approvals: { pending: 1, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n+    });\n+  });\n+});\n+\n+test(\"3. Approved\", async () => {\n+  await withServer(4733, async base => {\n+    await post(base, \"/webhook/event\", {\n+      id: \"health-approved\",\n+      payload: { to: \"test@example.com\" },\n+    });\n+    await waitForApproval(base, \"appr-health-approved\");\n+\n+    const approval = await post(base, \"/api/approvals/appr-health-approved/approve\");\n+    assert.strictEqual(approval.status, 200);\n+\n+    await assertHealth(base, {\n+      ok: true,\n+      queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 0 },\n+      approvals: { pending: 0, sent: 1, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n+    });\n+  });\n+});\ndiff --git a/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js b/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js\nindex cc106e5..9cd4e0e 100644\n--- a/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js\n+++ b/conformance/app/tests/health.test.js\n@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ test(\"1. on a fresh server, /health reports an empty queue\", async () => {\n   assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n     ok: true,\n     queue: { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 },\n+    approvals: { pending: 0, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n   });\n });\n \n@@ -83,6 +84,7 @@ test(\"1b. after an event is accepted, /health reports queue.pending incremented\n     assert.deepStrictEqual(await (await fetch(`${pendingBase}/health`)).json(), {\n       ok: true,\n       queue: { pending: 1, done: 0, dead: 0 },\n+      approvals: { pending: 0, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n     });\n   } finally {\n     pendingProc.kill(\"SIGKILL\");\n@@ -97,6 +99,7 @@ test(\"2. after a job completes, /health reports queue.done incremented by 1\", as\n   assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\n     ok: true,\n     queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 0 },\n+    approvals: { pending: 1, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n   });\n });\n \n@@ -107,5 +110,6 @@ test(\"3. after a job exhausts retries, /health reports queue.dead incremented by\n   assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\n     ok: true,\n     queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 1 },\n+    approvals: { pending: 1, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 },\n   });\n });\ndiff --git a/conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md b/conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md\nindex 7c8d97f..fc43718 100644\n--- a/conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md\n+++ b/conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md\n@@ -63