t needs to change. Full suite as of this run: 11 passed, 4 failed (all 4 failures are the `health.test.js` ones described above; `health-approvals.test.js` and `conformance.test.js` are fully green).\n+- 2026-07-12 21:10:01: builder run completed through the wrapper and committed implementation plus its ticket note in `5e201e0`; new contract tests pass 3/3 but the full suite is red (11 passed, 4 pre-existing T-101 health tests failed); State → Blocked-Escalated; cost $0.6861495. Javier must decide whether the frozen additive contract stands and authorize test-author updates to `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js`, or send T-102 back to planner for a revised contract.\n+- 2026-07-12: operator decision — the frozen additive T-102 contract stands; test-author is authorized to update only the exact-match `/health` expectations in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js` to include the frozen `approvals` object; State → In progress.\n+- 2026-07-12: dispatch stopped because mandatory `next-stage.sh --ticket T-102` returned `RUN reviewer`, not `RUN test-author`; State → Blocked-Escalated. Javier must reconcile the sequencer/bookkeeping so it names the authorized test-author correction; no role run was launched.\n+- 2026-07-12: operator resolution — no state surgery is needed; the frozen additive contract stands, the stale pre-T-102 exact-match assertions in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js` are the fault, and `RUN reviewer` is the legal adjudication step; State → In progress.\n+- 2026-07-12 21:14:32: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — update only the four stale exact-match `/health` expected bodies in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js` to include the frozen `approvals` object with scenario-appropriate counts; implementation and new tests conform; cost $0.1776.\n+- 2026-07-12: dispatch refused before the authorized test-author fix because the mandatory sequencer reported `REFUSE reviewer ran 1 time(s) but only 0 verdict(s) are logged on /Users/sofiagonzalez/Projec